{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The algebraic connectivity λ₂ (Fiedler 1973): the second smallest eigenvalue of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Laplacian L (of the normalized Laplacian N with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"normalized"},{"type":"text","text":"), 0 exactly when the graph is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not connected (a weight-0 edge does not connect)."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/algebraicConnectivity(normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"algebraicConnectivity"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"normalized"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":" = false, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1e-8, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxIterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization, the null space projected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, from a fixed start vector: on σI − L (σ twice the largest weighted degree; 2I − N with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"normalized"},{"type":"text","text":") while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on L⁺ by shift-invert, each product a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz pair is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepted when its residual is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · λ₂, so λ₂ is relative to itself however"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the weights spread; the value is then the vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dense solver below 64 vertices. O((n + m) · products) time; 31 n "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s (34 n from 5,000"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, for the polynomial filter), and on the shift-invert path O(n + m) more for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"solver."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"At least two vertices, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":", when given, is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at least 1.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note"},{"name":"Throws","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" when the Lanczos run on L⁺ spends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" matrix–vector"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"products (1,000 when nil) without converging, with the products spent and the Ritz"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"residual relative to 1\/λ₂. The run on σI − L that may come first hands over to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 + 20√n products or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whichever is smaller. Each shift-invert product is a conjugate-gradient solve that throws,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with its own iterations and relative residual, after 20,000 + 2n. Below 64 vertices the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dense solver answers and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" is unused. Only a tolerance below rounding has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reached the default limits in the measurements."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE21algebraicConnectivity10normalized9tolerance13maxIterationsSdSb_SdSiSgtAA13NoConvergenceVYKF","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"algebraicConnectivity"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"normalized"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxIterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"title":"algebraicConnectivity(normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"SpectralGraphTheory","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"FiedlerVector.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector.swift#L97"}},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/algebraicconnectivity(normalized:tolerance:maxiterations:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","title":"SpectralGraphTheory","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/NoConvergence":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/noconvergence","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","title":"NoConvergence","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The error an iterative method throws when it uses up its iteration limit without meeting its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stopping rule."}]},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/Spectr